{"id": "EUVD-2026-85888", "enisaUuid": "46ceaef0-a75d-330c-a218-74892e171cf8", "description": "IBM PowerVM Hypervisor FW1120.00 through FW1120.01, FW1110.00 through FW1110.31, FW1060.00 through FW1060.81, and FW950.00 through FW950.H3 is affected by a vulnerability in the RTAS firmware-to-OS interface. An attacker with administrator-level (root) access to a logical partition can send a specially crafted request to partition firmware, causing the partition to crash and become unavailable. Other partitions on the same managed system are not affected.", "datePublished": "2026-09-24T14:03:13", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-24T14:56:11", "baseScore": 5.1, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:H/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:L/A:H", "references": ["https://www.ibm.com/support/pages/node/7289124"], "aliases": ["GHSA-rw7q-c636-gvfq", "CVE-2026-17413"], "assigner": "ibm", "epss": 0.11, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "04892a7c-5646-362a-b35d-6ba063e561a1", "product": {"name": "PowerVM Hypervisor", "vendor": {"name": "IBM"}}, "product_version": "FW1120.00 \u2264FW1120.01"}, {"id": "06fde7fe-77ea-3855-a553-d8a7c5c8d15a", "product": {"name": "PowerVM Hypervisor", "vendor": {"name": "IBM"}}, "product_version": "FW1110.00 \u2264FW1110.31"}, {"id": "c14d9ced-2ef2-3ce9-bda2-2be231c398f4", "product": {"name": "PowerVM Hypervisor", "vendor": {"name": "IBM"}}, "product_version": "FW1060.00 \u2264FW1060.81"}, {"id": "e7549aa6-5959-3e3f-9889-fd4d5b7bfe24", "product": {"name": "PowerVM Hypervisor", "vendor": {"name": "IBM"}}, "product_version": "FW950.00 \u2264FW950.H3"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "cfa98536-f841-3d36-a9a8-d1970baa2493", "vendor": {"name": "IBM"}}], "isExploited": false}